cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this teaching material, please cite the tutorial and the relevant sources in REFERENCES.md."
type: software
title: "Graph Neural Networks for Passive Transient Source Localisation: An Interactive HKUST Tutorial"
authors:
  - family-names: "Waqar"
    given-names: "Muhammad"
    affiliation: "Hong Kong Metropolitan University"
date-released: 2026-11-04
abstract: >-
  A self-contained Jupyter teaching project that introduces graphs, adjacency,
  travel-time priors, input features, embeddings and message passing through
  passive hydraulic transient source localisation on the HKUST retained primary network.
  A compact graph neural network predicts an original pipe and a continuous
  position within it. The project includes prepared hydraulic signals,
  interactive explanations, training examples and optional local simulations.
keywords:
  - graph neural networks
  - hydraulic transients
  - passive source localisation
  - water distribution networks
  - Jupyter tutorial
  - TSNet
